# Exam track — Theme: Film & TV — Sub-lesson 3: Talking About It
# @question sentences: the examiner asks in Luxembourgish, the learner
# assembles the Luxembourgish answer (always en→lu).
#
# These are the user's real answers, gathered by interview on 2026-09-01 —
# do not "improve" or genericize them in a later editing pass. The point is
# that the learner rehearses what they will actually say in the Sproochentest.
#
# The @fill blocks carry frames that recur across any topic: well-causal,
# wann-conditional, obwuel-contrast, léiwer-wéi comparative, fir…ze purpose,
# dofir inversion, a number blank, a frequency adverb, and an Ech-mengen hedge.

@lesson T1.03 "Talking About Film & TV"

@word kucken = to watch
@word streamen = to stream
@word léinen = to borrow
@word eraussichen = to pick out
@word sech entspanen = to relax
@word abonéieren = to subscribe
@word oplueden = to upload
@word wiesselen = to switch
@word wielen = to choose
@word de Superheld = the superhero
@word d'Handlung = the plot
@word d'Sendung = the broadcast
@word de Programm = the program
@word d'Paus = the break
@word de Virdeel = the advantage
@word d'Gesellschaft = the company
@word d'Schlofzëmmer = the bedroom
@word de Kapp = the head
@word bequeem = convenient
@word deier = expensive

